        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4ec50e16-7e4c-5770-9098-62cbf1ca7713",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: ValuJet Airlines\n- Events: ValuJet Flight 592 crash\n- People: Candi Kubeck\n- Places: Miami, Everglades, Clayton County, Georgia, Eastern United States, Canada\n- Products: McDonnell-Douglas DC-9\n\nFacts:\n- ValuJet Airlines was an American low-cost carrier headquartered in unincorporated Clayton County, Georgia, and it operated regularly scheduled domestic and international flights in the Eastern United States and Canada during the 1990s.\n- Candalyn \"Candi\" Kubeck was born on May 10, 1961, and she was an American commercial airline pilot.\n- On May 11, 1996, ValuJet Flight 592, a ValuJet Airlines McDonnell-Douglas DC-9 departing Miami, crashed into the Everglades about 11 minutes after takeoff.\n- The ValuJet Flight 592 crash was caused by a fire in the cargo compartment that resulted from improperly stored cargo.\n- Candalyn \"Candi\" Kubeck died on May 11, 1996, and she was the captain of ValuJet Flight 592.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
